  <rules>
    <rule name="&apos;Ere We Go!" id="696e-ad7e-dc4b-ebbc" hidden="false">
      <description>If every model in a unit has this special rule, the unit can re-roll a single dice when determining its charge range. In addition, when a unit made up entirely of models with this special rule makes the Advance Reaction, they may add +D3 to their Initiative Characteristic when determining the number of inches they can move. This is in addition to any other modifiers such as from the Light Sub-type</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Mob Rule" id="4ee0-7679-ff6d-cf96" hidden="false">
      <description>A unit made up entirely of models with the Mob Rule special rule may count their Leadership as being equal to the number of models in the unit when taking any Leadership
tests, to a maximum of 10. If there are more than 10 models in the unit, the unit also gains the Stubborn special rule. Models with the Bulky (X) special rule count as a number of models equal to the value X
when determining mob size. (This rule does not affect Psychic Tests).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Mekaniak Kults" id="3b7b-476c-d327-0525" hidden="false">
      <description>A detachment that includes one or more Big Meks or Mega Big Meks may choose a
single Mekaniak Kult to apply to the detachment, chosen from the following:
•Kult of Speed
•Great Dread Mob
•Tellyporta Assault</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Waaagh!" id="1eb1-db1c-dccb-e22f" hidden="false">
      <description>Once per game, at the start of any of your turns after the first, a model with this special rule can, if he is your Warlord, call a Waaagh! On the turn he does so, all friendly units made up entirely of models with the ’Ere We Go! special rule may charge in the Assault phase even if they made a Run move in the same turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Waaagh! Energy" id="bda9-f2e9-c45a-e758" hidden="false">
      <description>A Weirdboy may increase his Leadership by 1 for the purpose of Psychic Tests if there are ten or more models with the &apos;Ere We Go! special rule in his unit.</description>
    </rule>
  </rules>
