    <selectionEntryGroup name="Power of the Waaagh!" id="2813-654b-f5e3-4ebb" hidden="false">
      <constraints>
        <constraint id="af4a-f091-ecea-d681" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="3"/>
        <constraint id="df45-b698-c220-63be" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" type="min" value="3"/>
      </constraints>
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry name="&apos;Eadbanger" id="d83e-3d34-01c7-22f5" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="7968-fb7d-ad1c-06d8" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
            <constraint id="6530-2557-c3c8-52ab" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="min" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="&apos;Eadbanger" id="355a-a363-1466-90e9" hidden="false" typeId="66fe-f217-d00c-847a" typeName="Weapon">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Range" typeId="1fc0-83ca-e978-5a16">24&quot;</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Strength" typeId="cb5e-ad7f-f63b-41cd">*</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="AP" typeId="1544-3a5e-d421-edf9">2</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Type" typeId="79ff-eaa1-5809-53f3">Assault 1, Blind, Frazzle, Pinning, Psychic Focus, Sniper</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Frazzle" id="1da7-5d60-a40e-f7ae" hidden="false">
              <description>Instead of rolling To Hit and To Wound normally, this weapon hits its target on a D6 roll of 2+ and the target of this attack must pass a Toughness test or suffer a Wound. Invulnerable saves and Damage Mitigation rolls may be taken as normal</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Psychic Focus" id="888c-0f10-24c8-20a0" hidden="false">
              <description>Before making any To Hit rolls with this weapon, the Psyker must make a Psychic check. If the Check is passed, then the Psyker may attack as normal using the profile shown for this weapon. If the Check is failed, then the Psyker suffers Perils of the Warp, and if the model is not removed as a casualty then it may attack as normal but may not use this weapon.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Aetheric Lightning" id="686b-a051-cc02-4370" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="2cc9-9c05-ffa9-b604" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
            <constraint id="65fa-937a-aabb-b42d" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="min" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Aetheric Lightning" id="3c6a-330b-f94a-5d6a" hidden="false" typeId="66fe-f217-d00c-847a" typeName="Weapon">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Range" typeId="1fc0-83ca-e978-5a16">18&quot;</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Strength" typeId="cb5e-ad7f-f63b-41cd">3</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="AP" typeId="1544-3a5e-d421-edf9">4</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Type" typeId="79ff-eaa1-5809-53f3">Assault 4, Force</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Warpath" id="d287-c91f-ca38-cf0a" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="a0d0-e99c-eb9a-4507" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
            <constraint id="9c94-d163-78ff-6df7" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="min" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Warpath" id="5078-94fb-c240-73de" hidden="false" typeId="479e-e1a8-1cd4-f3be" typeName="Psychic Ability">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Effect" typeId="e234-f7ad-e292-5d62">Instead of making a Shooting Attack, a Psyker with this Psychic Power may activate this Psychic Power. The Psyker and any model in a unit he has joined that has the ‘Ere We Go special rule increases their Attacks by +1 for the duration of the current player turn. When using this power, the controlling player may choose to have the Psyker take a Psychic check. If the Check is passed then both Weapon Skill and Attacks are increased by +1 for the duration of the current player turn. If the Check is failed, then the target unit gains no benefit and the Psyker suffers Perils of the
Warp</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
    </selectionEntryGroup>
    <selectionEntryGroup name="Warlord" id="b038-630c-2f77-8267" hidden="false">
      <constraints>
        <constraint id="644e-7740-3e2b-31f2" field="selections" scope="force" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
        <constraint id="593e-53e1-0289-62f6" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
      </constraints>
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry name="Prophet of the Waaagh!" id="d793-619e-f3e3-bd08" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule name="Prophet of the Waaagh!" id="95b4-6a20-ff10-66bc" hidden="false">
              <description>A Warlord with this Trait and any unit they have joined gain the Crusader and Stubborn
special rules. The Warlord also gains the Fear (1) special rule. If the Warlord already has the Fear (X) special rule or gains it by any other means, the value in brackets is increased by +1 instead. In addition, an army whose Warlord has this Trait may call a Waaagh! as long as the Warlord has not been removed as a casualty</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Brutal but Kunnin&apos;" id="8233-7dc9-462a-d21c" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule name="Brutal but Kunnin&apos;" id="eb43-6be8-e7ef-4ee1" hidden="false">
              <description>A Warlord with this Trait and any unit they have joined gain the Hatred special rule, and any Melee weapons
wielded by a Warlord with this Trait gain the Brutal (2) special rule. If the Warlord’s Melee weapons already have the Brutal (X) special rule (or otherwise gain it), the number in brackets is increased by +1 instead. In addition, an army whose Warlord has this Trait may call a Waaagh! as long as the Warlord has not been removed as a casualty</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Kunnin&apos; but Brutal" id="8a46-ba98-cfec-67bf" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule name="Kunnin&apos; but Brutal" id="1e3f-9935-e7cb-4320" hidden="false">
              <description>A Warlord with this Trait gains the It Will Not Die (5+) special rule, and the ranged weapons of the Warlord and any unit they have joined gain the More Dakka (1) special rule. If the Warlord’s or the unit’s ranged weapons already have the More Dakka (X) special rule (or otherwise gain it), the number in brackets is increased by +1 for that weapon instead. In addition, an army whose Warlord has this Trait may call a Waaagh! as long as the Warlord has not been removed as a casualty</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
    </selectionEntryGroup>
  </sharedSelectionEntryGroups>
</catalogue>
